---
description: Fixture loading is always fixtures :all, never a name list
alwaysApply: true
---

# Fixtures :all

Fixture loading is one universe. `fixtures :all` loads every YAML file under `test/fixtures/`. That directory is the source of truth. Do not encode an inclusion list of fixture names in Ruby. Lists drift every time a model or fixture file is added. There is no meaningful performance win.

```ruby
# bad
# fixtures :all
fixtures :organizations, :users
```

```ruby
# good
fixtures :all
```

Keep the single uncommented `fixtures :all` in `test/test_helper.rb`. Do not call `fixtures` again in individual tests.
